## Decisions the spec didn't pin down

- Comments are recognized after leading whitespace, since "lines starting with ; or #" and values have whitespace trimmed — an indented `; foo` is treated as a comment rather than an error.
- Comment markers only count at line start; no inline/trailing comment stripping (`k = a # b` keeps `a # b` as the value).
- An unquoted value that isn't fully wrapped in quotes keeps any quote characters as-is; only a value that starts *and* ends with `"` (length ≥ 2) is unwrapped.
- Sections only materialize when a key is added to them, and `[]` would reset to the empty section (edge case, untested).

